// test_typecheck_delayed_fwd.mkt
//
// PURPOSE: Verify that a closure body may contain a forward reference to a
// service member declared after the closure, without triggering a static
// check error.
//
// EXPECTED OUTCOME: PASSES all static checks (nameres, type checking,
// dependency analysis).
//
// RATIONALE: `f`'s body `fn () => a` is never executed eagerly during
// service initialization. The closure is a thunk -- its body is only
// evaluated when called. At call time, `a` is guaranteed to be initialized.
// Therefore the forward reference is safe and must be accepted.
//
// This is the canonical simplified example from GitHub Issue #173,
// contributed by @neurusL and confirmed in PR #120.
//
// Makefile target: test-forward-decls (expected: exit 0)

service s {
    def f = fn () => a; 
    var a = 0;
}
